peacemachine-dvd-ripper (1.0.9) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Run the HandBrake scan directly instead of through systemd-run. Reading the
    JSON back through a pipe from a systemd-run scope deadlocked on Debian: the
    window sat on "Scanning..." for ever while no HandBrake process existed.
    Encodes still get the 80%-CPU quota.

 -- William James Sova (C0D3D) <william@peacemachinestudios.com>  Sun, 15 Nov 2026 04:17:00 -0500

peacemachine-dvd-ripper (1.0.8) unstable; urgency=medium

  * The automatic scan now tries every optical drive until one yields titles.
    A virtual CD with an ISO in it looks like a disc to the kernel, so picking
    "the drive with media" could still choose the wrong one.

 -- William James Sova (C0D3D) <william@peacemachinestudios.com>  Sun, 15 Nov 2026 04:12:00 -0500

peacemachine-dvd-ripper (1.0.7) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Scan a disc that is already in the drive without being asked. When a drive
    with media is detected at startup the app fills the source and starts the
    scan itself, once per disc, never while a rip is running.

 -- William James Sova (C0D3D) <william@peacemachinestudios.com>  Sun, 15 Nov 2026 04:09:00 -0500

peacemachine-dvd-ripper (1.0.6) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Pick the drive that has a disc in it. A leftover installer ISO on sr0 used to
    win the auto-detect slot over the real DVD on sr1, so every scan failed with
    "no disc". Drives holding media now sort first.
  * README: libdvd-pkg needs Debian's "contrib" section, with the one-line fix.

 -- William James Sova (C0D3D) <william@peacemachinestudios.com>  Sun, 15 Nov 2026 04:06:00 -0500

peacemachine-dvd-ripper (1.0.5) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Fix the cairo bridge check from 1.0.4. It tried to import a name called
    "cairo" out of gi._gi_cairo, which does not exist, so the app decided the
    bridge was missing and skipped every cairo widget even when
    python3-gi-cairo was installed - blank spinner, blank blue binary. The check
    now imports gi._gi_cairo itself, which is what registers the converter.

 -- William James Sova (C0D3D) <william@peacemachinestudios.com>  Sun, 15 Nov 2026 03:59:00 -0500

peacemachine-dvd-ripper (1.0.4) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Add python3-gi-cairo: without PyGObject's cairo bridge the spinner, the blue
    binary, the rounded rules and the circle steppers threw "Couldn't find
    foreign struct converter for 'cairo.Context'" on every frame and drew
    nothing. Found on a Debian 13 test install.
  * Skip cairo drawing cleanly (and log once) if the bridge is ever missing,
    instead of a traceback per frame.

 -- William James Sova (C0D3D) <william@peacemachinestudios.com>  Sun, 15 Nov 2026 03:53:00 -0500

peacemachine-dvd-ripper (1.0.3) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Window controls are drawn as the house discs - round, black face, green
    ring - instead of GTK's default pills, so the app matches C0D3D's desktop
    on machines that have no hyprbars plugin.

